-- title:
--   Order of the Hecke multiplier at a pole of j
-- statement:
--   Let $k$ be a perfect field and let $N$ and $\ell$ be nonzero natural numbers with $\ell$ prime and $\ell \nmid N$. Write $\mathcal{F} = k(j(q), j(q^N))$ for the $k$-subfield of the Laurent series field $k((q))$ generated by the $j$-expansion $j(q)$ and its substitution $j(q^N)$, and let $R$ be the $k$-subfield of $k((q))$ generated by $j(q)$, $j(q^N)$, $j(q^{\ell})$ and $j(q^{N\ell})$; let $\bar\jmath \in \mathcal{F}$ denote $j(q)$. Two $k$-algebra maps $\mathcal{F} \to R$ are in play: $\alpha$, the inclusion, and $\beta$, induced by the substitution $q \mapsto q^{\ell}$ on Laurent series. It is assumed that $\mathcal{F}$ is algebraic over $k(\bar\jmath)$ and that $R$ is finite-dimensional over $k(\alpha\bar\jmath)$. Let $h \in R$ satisfy $d(\beta\bar\jmath) = h \cdot \alpha^{*}(d\bar\jmath)$ in $\Omega_{R/k}$, where $\alpha^{*}$ is the $k$-linear map $\Omega_{\mathcal{F}/k} \to \Omega_{R/k}$ induced by $\alpha$, and assume $d(\alpha\bar\jmath) \neq 0$ and $d(\beta\bar\jmath) \neq 0$. Let $y$ be a place of $R$ over $k$, that is, a proper valuation subring of $R$ containing the image of $k$ whose valuation ring is a principal ideal ring, with $\operatorname{ord}_y$ the associated normalised integer valuation. If $\operatorname{ord}_y(\alpha\bar\jmath) < 0$ and the absolute values of $\operatorname{ord}_y(\alpha\bar\jmath)$ and of $\operatorname{ord}_y(\beta\bar\jmath)$ are nonzero in $k$, then $$\operatorname{ord}_y h = \operatorname{ord}_y(\beta\bar\jmath) - \operatorname{ord}_y(\alpha\bar\jmath).$$
--
--   This is the cusp bookkeeping for the multiplier of the $\ell$-degeneracy correspondence on the modular function field: at a place where $\bar\jmath$ has a pole of order prime to the characteristic, the order of the Hecke multiplier is the difference of the two pole orders. It specialises [`ModularCurve.ord_heckeMultiplier_eq`](thm.html#ModularCurve.ord_heckeMultiplier_eq) to such places, the integrality hypotheses on $\alpha$ and $\beta$ being supplied by [`ModularCurve.heckeAlphaCIntegral_unconditional`](thm.html#ModularCurve.heckeAlphaCIntegral_unconditional) and [`ModularCurve.heckeBetaCIntegral_unconditional`](thm.html#ModularCurve.heckeBetaCIntegral_unconditional), and is used by [`ModularCurve.ord_heckeMultiplier_eq_of_ord_neg_of_eq_smul_map`](thm.html#ModularCurve.ord_heckeMultiplier_eq_of_ord_neg_of_eq_smul_map).
